# install-deps.allow — HQ's sanctioned global CLI dependencies.
#
# WHY: HQ's own install surface (core/scripts/setup.sh, the desktop installer)
# legitimately installs a small set of global CLIs with npm — qmd, the hq CLI,
# Claude Code. The supply-chain guard (.claude/hooks/block-unsafe-package-install.sh)
# hard-blocks every `npm install <pkg>` and points at pnpm + minimumReleaseAge,
# which is the wrong fix for a global CLI on a user machine and left agents
# unable to repair broken user installs.
#
# An entry listed here is allowed through the guard ONLY when installed
# GLOBALLY — `npm install -g` / `npm i -g` / `pnpm add -g` — and ONLY with an
# explicit version pin. The pin is reviewed in-repo: bumping it goes through PR
# review, which is the release-age gate for this surface. Non-global installs
# and unpinned installs are still blocked.
#
# Two entry forms, one per line, `#` starts a comment:
#   name@1.2.3   exact pin — only that exact version is allowed.
#   name@*       any EXPLICIT version pin is allowed (name@1.2.3). A bare
#                `name` or a dist-tag (name@latest, name@next) is still blocked.
#
# Referenced by: .claude/hooks/block-unsafe-package-install.sh
@tobilu/qmd@2.5.3
@indigoai-us/hq-cli@*
@anthropic-ai/claude-code@*
indigo-cli@*
